\section{Anonymisation}{

This is real data, processed so that it can be distributed. Specifically:

\itemize{
  \item Direct identifiers were removed: national id, names, phone numbers,
    email address, street address, employer name, IP address, date of birth.
    \code{client_age} carries what date of birth encoded.
  \item \code{application_id}, \code{client_id} and \code{loan_id} were
    re-mapped to new values, assigned in order of first appearance in time.
    Relationships between them are exact, but they no longer key into any
    production system. Because they are sequential, \code{application_id}
    sorts the same way as \code{app_created_at} -- convenient, and no more
    revealing than \code{app_created_at} itself.
  \item \strong{Every date was shifted by the same constant offset.}
    Intervals, day-of-month and day-of-week effects, seasonality and
    vintage ordering are all preserved; the calendar dates are not real.
    A separate 4-hour timezone correction was applied to the timestamp
